1. Definitions
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Licensor" means the copyright holder named above (GitHub user "_xyrz"), acting
for itself and, under Section 9, for the contributors.

"Software" means PolyLoader as provided by the Licensor under this License: its
source code, documentation, build scripts, website content and every compiled
or packaged form of it (such as jar files, installers and executables).

"You" means the person or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

"Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, derived from, or contains
the Software or a substantial part of it, in source or compiled form, including
modified versions, translations into another programming language, ports and
adaptations. Section 5 adds works produced by automated analysis.

"Mod" means a separate work that runs on the Software and interacts with it
only through the Software's documented public interfaces (the Java packages
dev.polyloader.api.*, the mod metadata file poly.mod.json, and the mod
development Gradle plugin), such as a "Poly Mod". A Mod is not a Derivative
Work merely because it uses those interfaces or names their classes and
methods.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software or a Derivative Work that is
intended for, or directed toward, commercial advantage or monetary
compensation, including:
  (a) selling, renting, leasing or sublicensing copies of the Software or of a
      Derivative Work, or charging for access to, download of, installation of
      or support for them;
  (b) including the Software or a Derivative Work in a product, bundle,
      modpack, launcher, hosting plan or other offering that is sold or that
      requires payment, a subscription or the purchase of anything else;
  (c) providing the Software or a Derivative Work to third parties as a paid
      service, including as a feature of commercial game server hosting;
  (d) using the Software or a Derivative Work inside a business to develop,
      operate or support a commercial product or service, other than the
      activities allowed in Section 3.2.

"Non-Commercial Purpose" means any purpose that is not Commercial Use.

"Distribute" means to make the Software or a Derivative Work available to
anyone other than You, by any means.

