5. Reverse engineering, automated analysis and AI systems
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 Study. You may read, run, debug and inspect the Software, and decompile or
disassemble its compiled forms, for Non-Commercial Purposes.

5.2 Automated reimplementation. As a condition of this License, You agree that
a work is a Derivative Work, whether or not it copies any code literally, if it
is produced by using the Software (or any part, output, documentation or
behaviour of it) as an input to a process of analysis, decompilation,
translation, transpilation, summarization and regeneration, or
reimplementation, whether performed by people, by automated tools, or by
artificial intelligence or machine learning systems (including tools that
"reverse engineer anything" or produce "clean room" rewrites), and the
resulting work reproduces the Software's expression, or its structure,
sequence and organization, or replaces the Software's functionality as a mod
loader or as an implementation of its public interfaces. Such a work is
subject to this License, including Section 3.

5.3 AI training and retrieval. You may not use the Software, in whole or in
part, as training, fine-tuning, distillation, evaluation or benchmark data, or
as retrieval or context material, for an artificial intelligence or machine
learning model or system that is used for Commercial Use or that is made
available to others for a fee. Use for Non-Commercial Purposes is allowed if
outputs that reproduce the Software are treated as Derivative Works under this
License.

5.4 No license laundering. You may not remove or alter license notices, or
present the Software or a Derivative Work as Your original work or as being
under other license terms, whether directly or through an automated tool.

5.5 Rights under law. This Section does not limit any right You have under
applicable law that cannot be restricted by agreement, such as the right to
analyse a program to achieve interoperability of an independently created
program. You may exercise such a right only to the extent the law allows.

